Package: vabaxos-voice
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, python3-numpy, python3-onnxruntime, libespeak-ng1, libsonic0, libpulse0, espeak-ng, speech-dispatcher, speech-dispatcher-espeak-ng, init-system-helpers
Description: Natural voices for VabaxOS (Kokoro)
 Kokoro, a natural-sounding neural voice, for Orca and every program that
 speaks through Speech Dispatcher (ADR-0019), chosen by the user (ADR-0030):
 the program Natural voice downloads the model (about 350 MB, checked with
 SHA-256), plays an example, measures this computer and says whether it is
 fast enough, and turns it on for Orca. eSpeak NG stays the desktop voice;
 without the model Kokoro's module speaks with eSpeak NG. Speed comes from
 Sonic, the first words of long sentences start at once, phrases already
 said are cached, and speech stops at once on every key.
